  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "Mistral3 image ingestion accepted one image at a time; this change adds list input without requiring equal-sized image embeddings.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_4f14a59ee58f407d9ad18a3c85a18000"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "Processing each list member through the existing single-image method preserves image-specific spatial parameters and satisfies Mistral3PatchMerger.forward's batch-size-one assertion. Unlike Gemma3's concatenated batch, this is sequential ingestion.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_4f14a59ee58f407d9ad18a3c85a18000", "call_88c36d82ca9c4f5190427a6a27d7361e", "call_2134c99de32e4c3ca1cf0f575f599ee1"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "Single-image calls retain their MMEmbedding return. A list returns an ordered list, including an empty list for empty input, and rejects a supplied text_alias. The existing multimodal example remains compatible because it calls the method separately for each image.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_4f14a59ee58f407d9ad18a3c85a18000", "call_c6b31617bc9a4185bfec7f628c6135f0", "call_79aa8167daca40b9b6b642d68e3e3905"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Read the Gemma3 batching and Mistral3 introduction entries. They establish the preceding list interface and the merger's singleton-batch precondition. The Mistral3 introduction also records an inherited resize-overflow observation.",
      "basis": "ancestor",
      "evidence": ["call_218684a3ae2946a895922f5828374b75", "call_2395a83a148c49db8a7aca6c3a6e42c1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That recorded overflow mechanism is no longer present in the inspected parent helper: it floors scaled dimensions before patch alignment. The task leaves that helper and its preprocessing caller unchanged.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_178efb3bd11a4044ace57d646e9c215c", "call_c6b31617bc9a4185bfec7f628c6135f0", "call_4f14a59ee58f407d9ad18a3c85a18000"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Issue #48, “`RuntimeError` when requesting logprobs with Gemma 3 models,” reports vocabulary/logit-width disagreement. Its relationship to this task is inferred solely from the shared gemma3.py path; the image-ingestion edits do not address its reported failure.",
      "basis": "inference",
      "evidence": ["call_2b60f89ccfd84b9bb0a377d4e57211ba", "call_a0f6764026114dfc9c8f23f9f3c015da"]
